    "created_at": "2017-12-01T23:26:41Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-12-01T23:26:41Z",
    "body": "Unfortunately, that's not a sufficient reason to add new features to the platform that are this special-cased. We have a general-purpose programming language for achieving general-purpose things; HTML is a specific vocabulary for common, semantic use cases, where having a markup language is valuable. Unless you can show us that this kind of session-end popup is as common as HTML elements like links, buttons, divs, and spans, it's not going to meet the bar for something that needs to be done in the declarative, semantic language of HTML.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
